codex
The revised regime is materially stronger: a separate HiGHS MILP check failed on 8/8 hard-regime instances at a 30-second limit, while the built-in exact DSATUR/DPLL search has now failed on 9/9 samples after one million nodes each. The full self-test is still running because those million-node attacks are deliberately part of the gate, not a cardinality proxy.
