Completed a Track A generator based on the paper’s Section 1 reduction.

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: 252 vertices, 5-regular, 50 switch rounds.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Exact DSATUR/DPLL: 0/8 after 1,000,001 nodes each.
- Bare, structural-hint, and placebo oracle arms: 0/3 solved each.
- Answer size: 254 characters, 252 atomic symbols.
- The README explicitly notes that fixed-3-coloring NP-completeness is worst-case evidence, not a proof of distributional hardness, and discusses known planted-coloring algorithms as a caveat. See the [source paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.08995) and related [planted-coloring analysis](https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05183).

